course: dictionary
lesson: 5699
title: Logical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Logical means following clear reasoning, so each step makes sense. Look for the clues in the sentence. «Prepositions are the least logical words in any language» tells you that their rules do not follow clear steps, so each country uses them differently.
explain: «Stations are big but logical.» Big does not mean confusing. In London you follow the line's name and colour, and the last station in your direction. Each step follows from the one before, so the system is logical.
explain: Logical can also mean sensible, the thing you would expect from the facts. On escalators you stand on the right so people in a hurry can walk on the left. That is the logical thing to do, because it follows from what people need.
fact: Logical means following clear and correct reasoning, so each step makes sense.
fact: Logical can also mean sensible and what you would expect, given the facts.
fact: A logical person thinks clearly and step by step.
fact: Useful phrases: "logical order", "logical thinking", and "it's logical that…".
fact: In computing, logical operations are AND, OR and NOT.
exercise: «Stations are big but logical.» What does logical mean here? | *Clear rules that make sense step by step | Funny and silly | Hard to find anything | Very big and tall
exercise: In a logic puzzle, what should a logical answer do? | Make a guess without any reason | *Follow from the facts given | Ignore the facts completely | Change the facts to suit you
exercise: Which is the logical thing to do on an escalator in London? | Sit down on the steps | *Stand on the right so people in a hurry can walk on the left | Stand on the left so you block people | Stop right at the top
test: All cats are animals. Tom is a cat. What is the logical conclusion? | *Tom is an animal | Tom is a train | Tom is a plant | Tom is a fish
test: Which sentence shows logical thinking? | Umbrellas are sold in shops, so I'll sleep in the bath. | *It's raining, so I'll take an umbrella. | The sun is shining, so I'll wear my wellies. | I'll take an umbrella because I like the colour blue.
exam: «Prepositions are the least logical words in any language.» What does this tell you? | They are never used in sentences | *Their rules do not follow clear steps, so countries use them differently | They are all nouns | Their rules are clear, so every country uses them the same way
